  "flags": [
    {
      "page": 2,
      "what": "The PDF prints one Arabian Tribes warband list (pages 2-4) with three tribes - Ghutani, Muzil and Turjuk - that share its choice of warriors, fighters, profiles, prices and equipment lists and differ only in their Special Rules and their skill table. Our data holds the three as three warband types, so each is a source file of its own, the shared parts repeated and the differences carried."
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "what": "An Arabian Tribe warband needs at least 3 models: our templates hold no minimum, so it is not imported."
    },
    {
      "page": 3,
      "what": "The three skill tables' ticks are glyphs the reading-order text drops; read from the -layout text's tick columns and checked against page 3 as an image. The tables have five columns and no Special column, so the tribes have no skill group of their own."
    },
    {
      "page": 3,
      "what": "The Arabian Tribe and Townsmen lists print Mace and Hammer as two lines at 3 dinars each; both are our Club, Mace or Hammer, so each list carries one line for them."
    },
    {
      "page": 4,
      "what": "The Scholar's Theology field gives him Holy skills, and the Occult field makes him a Lesser Magic wizard. We hold no Holy skill group and a field is picked per model, so neither is a skill group or a spell lore on the Scholar: the choice stays in his rule."
    },
    {
      "page": 4,
      "what": "No maximum profile and no henchmen group sizes are printed: the warband takes our Human race."
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "what": "The Ghutani may hire up to 5 Flagellants as henchmen. No Flagellant profile or price is printed here, so no fighter is added and the rule carries it."
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "what": "\"Ghutani scholar fields of study may only be poetry or theology\" narrows the Scholar's own Field of Scholarship rule, so it sits in that rule rather than in a warband rule."
    }
  ]
}
